  "body": "Update the `show the picker, if applicable` algorithm for `<input type=\"file\">` to pass `element's node navigable` to `WebDriver BiDi file dialog opened` and handle the returned `file dialog behavior struct` (`accepted` and `paths`) defined in https://github.com/w3c/webdriver-bidi/pull/1193.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * [Chromium](https://github.com/w3c/webdriver-bidi/pull/1193)\n- [ ] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * Companion WPT RFC: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/rfcs/pull/246\n   * Companion WPT PR: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64840\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * WebDriver BiDi: https://github.com/w3c/webdriver-bidi/pull/1193\n   * Chromium: https://crbug.com/346563686\n   * Gecko: N/A\n   * WebKit: N/A\n   * Deno (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, module resolution, web workers, and web storage): N/A\n   * Node.js (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, and module resolution): N/A\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: N/A\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n### Companion PRs & RFC\n- WebDriver BiDi (`browser.setFileDialogBehavior`): https://github.com/w3c/webdriver-bidi/pull/1193\n- WebDriver BiDi (`browser.createTemporaryDirectory`): https://github.com/w3c/webdriver-bidi/pull/1202\n- File System Access (`showOpenFilePicker` / `showSaveFilePicker` / `showDirectoryPicker`): https://github.com/WICG/file-system-access/pull/477\n- WPT RFC (`test_driver.set_file_picker_behavior` & `test_driver.create_temporary_directory`): https://github.com/web-platform-tests/rfcs/pull/246\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13197/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 5:52 AM UTC (5bd9a5e)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13197/a7f6aed...5bd9a5e/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 5:52 AM UTC (5bd9a5e)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13197/input.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 5:52 AM UTC (5bd9a5e)\">/input.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13197/a7f6aed...5bd9a5e/input.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 5:52 AM UTC (5bd9a5e)\">diff</a> )",
